=== ANGLE 6: is measS7 a MIN-CUT (single weakest sector) or a genuine product? ===

Compare 1-measS7 (true uncovered) vs sum_r miss_r (union bound) vs max_r miss_r (min-cut):
  k=8 consec: measS7=0.3272 uncovered=0.6728 | sum_r miss=1.6041  max_r miss=0.3347  | union/true=2.384 mincut/true=0.497
  k=9 consec: measS7=0.4162 uncovered=0.5838 | sum_r miss=1.3813  max_r miss=0.2932  | union/true=2.366 mincut/true=0.502
  k=10 consec: measS7=0.5045 uncovered=0.4955 | sum_r miss=1.1931  max_r miss=0.2525  | union/true=2.408 mincut/true=0.510
  => mincut/true ~1 means ONE sector dominates failure (min-cut model exact);
     <<1 means many sectors jointly fail (genuine product, no single bottleneck).

ANGLE 6b: does consec minimize max_r miss_r (= maximize the weakest sector's survival)?
  k=8: consec max_r miss=0.3347 | 7/60 random configs have SMALLER max-miss (beat consec)
  k=9: consec max_r miss=0.2932 | 13/60 random configs have SMALLER max-miss (beat consec)
  => 0 beats: consec IS the max-min (min-cut LP optimum). >0: min-cut model not the extremal certificate.

